\subsection{Verification Results Summary}
All storylines pass validation with:
\begin{itemize}
	\item 20+ nodes (requirement satisfied: Classic 30, Survival 20, Pack 20)
	\item 5+ endings (requirement satisfied: Classic 13, Survival 5, Pack 5)
	\item All paths validated (requirement satisfied: 13+5+5 = 23 total paths)
	\item No unreachable endings or broken paths
\end{itemize}

The Validator tool confirmed that all decisions lead to logical outcomes and all endings are accessible through valid game choices.

\section{Conclusion and Future Work}

The Wolf Pack Survival Adventure Game successfully demonstrates practical applications of fundamental data structures in an engaging gaming context. The project meets or exceeds all requirements specified in TeamA.txt, including:

\begin{itemize}
	\item Binary decision tree with 20+ nodes (implemented: 30 nodes)
	\item Priority queue for event management
	\item Linked lists for inventory and pack systems
	\item Stack for undo functionality
	\item Queue for action sequencing
	\item GUI interface with Qt6
	\item Save/load functionality
	\item Multiple storylines and endings
\end{itemize}

\textbf{Achievements:}
\begin{itemize}
	\item Exceeded minimum requirements (30+ nodes vs 20 required, 23 endings vs 5 required)
	\item Three distinct storylines (Classic, Survival, Pack)
	\item Difficulty-scaled inventory system with starting supplies and random drops
	\item New scavenging scenarios with difficulty-based item rewards
	\item Comprehensive testing with Validator tool
	\item Enhanced UI with achievements and stat tracking
\end{itemize}

\textbf{Future Improvements:}
\begin{itemize}
	\item Additional storylines and scenarios
	\item Enhanced graphics and animations
	\item Sound effects and background music
	\item Online multiplayer pack survival mode
	\item Procedural generation for infinite scenarios
\end{itemize}

The project demonstrates strong integration of computer science fundamentals with creative storytelling, providing an educational and entertaining experience.

\textbf{Acknowledgments:} Developed as a final project for Data Structures Lab, demonstrating practical applications of CS concepts in game development.

